ave that right uh  what's next for your character can you  even talk  like i don't even know um  you guys know this come on now i can't  tell you  come on samir give us something well  maura escaped from gillard we we  yes moya escaped from gilead in in  season one and there's um been a journey  um and i can't tell you nothing  does she find happiness um you know what  that's a great question actually i think  that that's a real question in her whole  arc as a character on the show um being  in a place like that with so much trauma  and escaping and now you're a refugee  it's there's so many things to find  happiness there's so many blocks in your  way um  so i think that's actually i really love  that you said that i think that moira's  journey is like a journey to find  happiness now you have said that you  feel it's a responsibility to show young  lgbtq  kids  what's possible why did you feel like  that was your responsibility  um  i think  there were some shoes that were given to  me in the very beginning of my career  that i thought were too big for me  um and i didn't want to step in them i  felt like  this is just too much for me and when i  made the decision to  say no i'm gonna step into this role i'm  gonna i'm gonna make a decision and have  my wife and i be on the cover of martha  martha stewart weddings because we're a  queer couple and i want to show people  what's possible some queer person in the  middle of the country that has never  seen anything like this so  i it's  it it felt like a  maybe a choice to to take this on and  have it be my responsibility but i don't  even feel like it's really a choice i  feel like this is what i'm supposed to  be doing and that choice has given  people strength so we appreciate you  thank you so much for joining us samara  wiley you're the best thank you we'll be  right back samira thank you

